 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:50:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx471: the sensor reads out RGGB

The mode advertised SGRBG10, but with no flip the IMX471 reads out an
RGGB pattern: a raw frame of the Nothing Phone (1) front camera has its
two matching greens at positions (0,1) and (1,0), and the mainline
driver lists SRGGB10 for the unflipped orientation. Debayering it as
GRBG gave a green/magenta cast and coloured blocks all over the image.

Advertise SRGGB10.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
index d5775cf05..dc7f547c5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
@@ -305,7 +305,7 @@ static const struct imx471_mode supported_mode = {
 	.vblank_max = 1522 - 648, // FIXME: need recheck(AI): min(frame_length_lines) - min(height)
 	.pclk = 137000000, // VTPXCK x 4
 	.link_freq_idx = 0,
-	.code = MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SGRBG10_1X10,
+	.code = MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SRGGB10_1X10,
 	.reg_list = {
 		.num_of_regs = ARRAY_SIZE(mode_2304x1728_regs),
 		.regs = mode_2304x1728_regs,
-- 
2.47.3

